<rss version="2.0"><channel><title>Opto-Hot · 光学元件与成像</title><link>https://opto-hot-a455-d3g2s3dt865d86640.webapps.tcloudbase.com/#/all</link><description>光学元件与成像</description><lastBuildDate>2026-09-25T09:29:45.289437+00:00</lastBuildDate><item><title>Real-Time Event-Based Optical Camera Communication at 80 kbit/s over a 320 m Outdoor Link with 120{\deg} Field-of-View</title><link>https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.29776</link><description>arXiv:2609.29776v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: We demonstrate an event-based optical camera communication system using a 120{\deg} field-of-view sensor. In daylight, three transmitting nodes achieve an aggregate 240 kbit/s, with individual links reaching 106 kbit/s at 1 m and 80 kbit/s at 320 m. Our results, establish a new baseline for event-OCC.</description><guid isPermaLink="false">cdf6c23727cd</guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T09:29:45.289437+00:00</pubDate><source>arXiv 光学与光子学 (physics.optics)</source><category>光学元件与成像</category></item><item><title>Angular-Channel Capacity and Nonlocal Wavefront Engineering for Phased-Array--Lens Systems</title><link>https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30060</link><description>arXiv:2609.30060v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Wide-angle beam steering with high directivity is fundamentally limited by diffraction, restricting the scan performance of phased-array systems. Here, we establish the bounds governing beam steering with high directivity in phased-array--lens systems and show that nonlocal dielectric metalenses can operate close to these limits. Unlike conventional metalenses that suppress mutual coupling, our approach exploits nonlocal electromagnetic interaction</description><guid isPermaLink="false">e7b09fb23453</guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T09:29:45.289437+00:00</pubDate><source>arXiv 光学与光子学 (physics.optics)</source><category>光学元件与成像</category></item><item><title>光瞳函数→PSF→MTF: 光学评价的三级数值链</title><link>https://optics.ofweek.com/2026-09/ART-250006-11000-30704750.html</link><description></description><guid isPermaL